# /brainstorm

Turn an idea or problem into an approved specification before building.
{% if modules.speckit %}Derive the tier first (`docs/process/risk-tiers.md`) — Tier 0/1 takes the
quick flow, no spec artifacts. For Tier 2+: read `PRODUCT.md` and the
decision records for the touched area as constraints, then run
`/speckit-specify` and iterate `/speckit-clarify` until no
`[NEEDS CLARIFICATION]` marker survives (the clarification gate blocks
markers from reaching plan/tasks).

**Issue at idea time, not at plan time.** Before specifying, create the
tracking issue (title + one-paragraph idea) — the human's influence window
is the spec/design stage, and an unpublished idea cannot be influenced. The
spec records its `issue: #N` line (the issues gate enforces it), and once
the spec stands (clarify done), publish it to the issue:
`python scripts/process/publish_and_prune.py --stage <feature-dir>` — a
read-only snapshot comment the human can react to. Read new issue comments
before `/plan`: they are clarify input, not archaeology.

See `docs/process/modules/speckit.md` for the full flow. Do not start
implementation before approval.
{% else %}Read `docs/process/workflow.md` and, for new or unclear projects, start with
`docs/process/start-here.md`. Ask a few targeted questions, summarize
assumptions, name trade-offs, and write the agreed design to a spec file using
the scaffold in `docs/process/design-template.md`. Mark anything underspecified
as `[NEEDS CLARIFICATION: <question>]` instead of guessing; resolve every
marker before approval. Do not start implementation before approval.
{% endif %}
Next: `/plan`.
